course: dictionary
lesson: 706
title: Sharp words: barb
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A barb is a sharp point that sticks out backwards, so it is hard to pull out. Read the clues around the word. «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out; an adult or doctor removes it, because the barb tears skin.» The clues are hook, finger and tears skin, so a barb is a sharp backward point.
explain: Barb can also mean an unkind remark that is meant to hurt someone. Which meaning fits depends on the sentence. A barb on a hook is a piece of metal, but a barb in a conversation is a sharp, mean comment. Always ask: does this word describe an object, or what someone says?
explain: Use the swap check. Put "sharp point" or "unkind remark" into the sentence in place of barb and see which one still makes sense. If the sentence is about a fish, a bee or a fence, it is the sharp point. If it is about a friend's words, it is the unkind remark.
fact: A barb is a sharp point that sticks out backwards, so it is hard to pull out.
fact: «A honeybee's barbed sting stays in the skin» because the barbs catch on the skin.
fact: «Barbed» means having barbs, as in «barbed wire».
fact: A barb can also be an unkind remark that is meant to hurt someone.
fact: A porcupine's quills have tiny barbs that work their way into skin; porcupines cannot shoot their quills.
exercise: «A fish hook stuck in a finger is not pulled out; an adult or doctor removes it, because the barb tears skin.» Why should a doctor remove the hook? | Because fish hooks can fly | Because hooks are always made of gold | Because the barb makes the hook shine | *Because the barb tears the skin when it is pulled out
exercise: Ellie says, «That comment was a real barb.» What does barb mean here? | A soft, warm feather | *An unkind remark meant to hurt | A sharp point on a fish hook | A kind gift from a friend
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Most American tarantulas flick itchy barbed hairs at enemies» that means having barbs. | *barbed | hairs | tarantulas | American
test: Farmers often put barbed wire on fences. Why should you climb over a barbed wire fence at a gate instead of pushing through it? | Barbed wire is soft and warm | *Barbed wire can cut you | Barbed wire makes a nice noise | Barbed wire is for kids to play with
test: What is the barb on a stingray's tail for? | To ring a bell | To hold a fish hook | *For defence, against enemies | To dig in the sand for worms
exam: Ruth says, «Your joke was a barb, and it hurt Sam.» What is the best meaning of barb here? | A sharp point on a fish hook | A round glass bead | *An unkind remark | A bee's sting
